;;; A one-room fixture world for the reach checker's carry model
;;; (t-c53681): a softlock that a checker searching each carry set only
;;; from the start passes.
;;;
;;; The ledge (cols 9-14, standing row 4) is four tiles above the floor, out
;;; of a held jump's 3.25; a ring-stone keyed to H2 at (8,8) is the step up to
;;; it. H2 lies on the ledge. East of the ledge is a pit four deep in smooth
;;; rock, whose only way out is a second H2 stone at (15,8), a step back up.
;;;
;;; Carrying nothing, every cell is reached and leads back: the stones are
;;; steps. Carrying H2, both stones are open (air), so from the start the
;;; ledge and the pit are out of reach, and a search from the start never
;;; looks at them. But a player who takes H2 on the ledge is there carrying
;;; it: from the ledge they can drop west to the floor (so "picked up, is
;;; there a way back from the harmonic's cell?" says yes), or drop east into
;;; the pit, whose step has gone. That is a softlock, and the checker must
;;; report it as a trap carrying H2.
(start region: stonefen room: (0 0) cell: (2 8))

(palette
  (sky-1 "#8fa3b3" "sky") (stone-1 "#5d5a55" "rock") (stone-2 "#7a766f" "rock lit"))

(region stonefen
  name: "Stone fen"
  bounds: ((0 0) (0 0))
  bed: "reedfen-bed"
  bed-channels: (wind water reeds drone)
  palette: (sky-1 stone-1 stone-2)
  roster: ()
  moments: ()
  gives: ((overtone 2)))
